Name: EasyList and EasyPrivacy
URL: https://easylist.to/
Version: fetched at build time
Update Mechanism: Manual
License: CC-BY-SA-3.0
License File: LICENSE
Security Critical: no
Shipped: yes

Description:
Rio's ad and tracker blocker (docs/chromium/m7.md) is compiled from EasyList
(https://easylist.to/easylist/easylist.txt) and EasyPrivacy
(https://easylist.to/easylist/easyprivacy.txt). scripts/chromium/fetch-filter-lists.mjs
fetches both before each build, and scripts/chromium/blocker/build.ts turns them
into the rules the overlay pak carries. Credit: The EasyList authors
(https://easylist.to/).

The lists are dual licensed under GPL-3.0-or-later and CC BY-SA 3.0 Unported or
later; Rio uses them under CC BY-SA 3.0, as Chromium's own copy of EasyList does
(third_party/subresource-filter-ruleset). LICENSE is that copy's licence file:
the EasyList repository notice followed by the CC BY-SA 3.0 legal code.

This directory holds no code. It exists so tools/licenses/licenses.py, which
lists every directory under a third_party directory, puts the lists on
chrome://credits.

Local Modifications:
The rules are converted to declarativeNetRequest rules and cosmetic selectors;
filters the converter cannot express are dropped.
